section.sourcecode:
cpoe-war = #6.1129791826(attestation-result) ; "CWAR"
attestation-result = { 1 => uint, ; version (MUST be 1) 2 => hash-value, ; evidence-ref 3 => verdict, ; appraisal verdict 4 => attestation-tier, ; assessed assurance level 5 => uint, ; chain-length 6 => uint, ; chain-duration (seconds) ? 7 => entropy-report, ? 8 => forgery-cost-estimate, ? 9 => [+ absence-claim], ; (max 100) ? 10 => [* tstr], ; warnings (max 100) 11 => bstr, ; verifier-signature (COSE_Sign1) 12 => pop-timestamp, ; created ? 13 => forensic-summary, ? 14 => confidence-tier, ? 15 => effort-attribution, }
effort-attribution = { 1 => float32, ; human-fraction 2 => uint, ; human-checkpoints 3 => uint, ; receipt-checkpoints ? 4 => uint, ; tool-attributed-chars ? 5 => uint, ; total-chars }
verdict = &( authentic: 1, inconclusive: 2, suspicious: 3, invalid: 4, )
forensic-summary = { 1 => uint, ; flags-triggered 2 => uint, ; flags-evaluated 3 => uint, ; affected-checkpoints 4 => uint, ; total-checkpoints ? 5 => [+ forensic-flag], ; (max 200) }
forensic-flag = { 1 => tstr, ; mechanism (e.g. "SNR", "CLC") 2 => bool, ; triggered 3 => uint, ; affected-windows 4 => uint, ; total-windows }
; In the forensic-flag structure, "windows" refers to individual ; checkpoints. The affected-windows field is the count of checkpoints ; where the forensic mechanism triggered; total-windows is the total ; number of checkpoints evaluated by that mechanism.
entropy-report = { 1 => float32, ; timing-entropy (bits/sample) 2 => float32, ; revision-entropy (bits) 3 => float32, ; pause-entropy (bits) 4 => bool, ; meets-threshold }
forgery-cost-estimate = { 1 => float32, ; c-swf 2 => float32, ; c-entropy 3 => float32, ; c-hardware 4 => float32, ; c-total 5 => cost-unit, }
cost-unit = &( usd: 1, cpu-hours: 2, )
absence-claim = { 1 => absence-type, 2 => time-window, 3 => tstr, ; claim-id ? 4 => any, ; threshold 5 => bool, ; assertion }
absence-type = &( computationally-bound: 1, monitoring-dependent: 2, environmental: 3, )
time-window = { 1 => pop-timestamp, ; start 2 => pop-timestamp, ; end }
; Behavioral Baseline Verification baseline-verification = { 1 => baseline-digest / null, ; null during enrollment 2 => session-behavioral-summary, ? 3 => bstr, ; digest-signature (COSE_Sign1) }
baseline-digest = { 1 => uint, ; version (MUST be 1) 2 => uint, ; session-count 3 => uint, ; total-keystrokes 4 => streaming-stats, ; iki-stats 5 => streaming-stats, ; cv-stats 6 => streaming-stats, ; hurst-stats 7 => [9*9 float32], ; aggregate-iki-histogram 8 => streaming-stats, ; pause-stats 9 => bstr .size 32, ; session-merkle-root (MMR) 10 => confidence-tier, ; baseline maturity 11 => pop-timestamp, ; computed-at 12 => bstr .size 32, ; identity-fingerprint }
session-behavioral-summary = { 1 => [9*9 float32], ; iki-histogram 2 => float32, ; iki-cv 3 => float32, ; hurst exponent 4 => float32, ; pause-frequency 5 => uint, ; duration-secs 6 => uint, ; keystroke-count }
streaming-stats = { 1 => uint, ; count 2 => float32, ; mean 3 => float32, ; m2 (Welford's running variance) 4 => float32, ; min 5 => float32, ; max }
; Receipts (Composition and Tool Attribution) receipt = self-receipt / tool-receipt
self-receipt = { 1 => tstr, ; tool-id 2 => hash-value, ; output-commit 3 => hash-value, ; evidence-ref 4 => pop-timestamp, ; transfer-time }
tool-receipt = { 1 => tstr, ; tool-id 2 => hash-value, ; output-commit ? 3 => hash-value, ; input-ref 4 => pop-timestamp, ; issued-at 5 => bstr, ; tool-signature (COSE_Sign1) ? 6 => uint, ; output-char-count }
; Shared type definitions reproduced from [CPoE-Protocol] for reader ; convenience. In case of conflict, [CPoE-Protocol] is authoritative. pop-timestamp = uint ; epoch milliseconds hash-value = { 1 => hash-algorithm, 2 => bstr, ; digest (length per algorithm) } compact-ref = { 1 => hash-algorithm, 2 => bstr .size (8..32), ; truncated-digest 3 => uint, ; prefix-length } hash-algorithm = &( sha-256: 1, sha-384: 2, sha-512: 3, ) confidence-tier = &( population-reference: 1, emerging: 2, established: 3, mature: 4, ) attestation-tier = &( software-only: 1, ; T1 / AAL1 attested-software: 2, ; T2 / AAL2 hardware-bound: 3, ; T3 / AAL3 hardware-hardened: 4, ; T4 / LoA4 )

section.t:
Checkpoints containing a verified tool-receipt are excluded from
forensic mechanisms that assume continuous human authorship (see
).

li.t:
ear.verifier-id: derived from the Verifier's signing key
identity in the verifier-signature COSE_Sign1 header (per
)

State matching: final content hash match required;
intermediate content hash progression SHOULD be
verified for monotonic growth.

Forensic assessment: all T3 requirements;
cross-correlation analysis between entropy and SNR
required. QR presence challenge RECOMMENDED.
